From 604e708872f141aa1eda572d43c00fc2c05d483d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:07:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] wip/kv-residency B-A: the attendance pool for the
 attention KV (mirror + pool + page table + resolve)

LLAMA_KV_REGION_POOL=<cells> (unset/0 = off, byte-identical): the attention KV lives twice --
a pinned host MIRROR that is authoritative and cell-indexed (every existing path, the writers
included, works on it unchanged) and a compact DEVICE POOL of pages of one indexer block, with a
page table block -> slot.  A decode step resolves its top-k selection through the table
(GGML_OP_KV_POOL: mark / claim / map / fill) and the QSA reader gathers K/V at the pool slots
(ggml_flash_attn_qsa_set_kv_idx) while the mask and visibility keys stay cell-indexed.

The writer rule is what makes it exact with no invalidation: writes land in the mirror, declared
pages are re-filled from it before the attention reads (the batch's written pages included), and
an eviction costs nothing.

Measured (Flash-Next IQ3_XXS, 1 GPU, -ncmoe 48, q8_0, -c 65536, 51 475 depth, sparse decode):
pool == the resident sparse arm byte-identically (854 chars 43b30de151b9, -n 64) at 4104 pages
(16416 cells/layer, 71.5 MiB), 89.7 % hit rate; the pool's own verify kernel reports 0 mismatches.
A 204 MiB pool is 1/12 of the resident KV's VRAM.

Three defects found and fixed on the way, each of which the text caught:
 1. a claim could evict a page the SAME launch still reads -- phases are now mark-then-claim, and a
    slot marked for this launch is never a victim;
 2. claim ATTEMPTS (one per id) wrapped the round-robin cursor on a 4-row batch, so two blocks shared
    a slot and a just-resolved block went unresident: the block list is deduplicated through the
    table CAS, so only DISTINCT blocks consume a slot;
 3. the fill list lived in a transient device-pool allocation, which a captured graph bakes -- the
    replay then wrote into whatever op had been handed that block.  It lives in the counters tensor now.

Campaign branch only; nothing leaves wip/.
